Package: methylQC
Title: QC and Preprocessing Pipeline for Illumina DNA Methylation Arrays
Version: 1.2.0
Authors@R: person("Brian", "Chen", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "brianchen450k@gmail.com")
Description: Two-stage QC pipeline for Illumina Infinium DNA methylation
    arrays (EPIC, EPICv2, 450K). Stage 1 streams samples through SeSAMe
    openSesame (prep code "QCDPB": quality masking, channel inference,
    dye-bias correction, pOOBAH detection p-values, and noob background
    correction), computes per-sample QC metrics (detection rate,
    intensity, Horvath epigenetic age, sex chromosome intensities), and
    extracts SNP probe betas. Stage 2 flags samples and probes, generates
    a multi-page QC report PDF, runs EpiDISH cell-type deconvolution as a
    purity check on blood-derived tissues, and outputs a consolidated
    sample sheet. Unmasked, noob-corrected beta and M-value matrices are
    output with separate quality-mask and detection p-value matrices.
    Users apply their own exclusion criteria via apply_mask(), which
    supports optional similarity-based k-NN imputation. Optional EPICv2
    replicate de-duplication and probe-ID harmonization to legacy
    platforms is provided via harmonize_epicv2().
